-- title:
--   Sums over prefixes and retained embeddings
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals.
--
--   1. **Supported reindexing.** If $f$ vanishes outside the image of an embedding $e:A\to B$, then
--   $$
--   \sum_{b\in B}f(b)=\sum_{a\in A}f(e(a)) .
--   $$
--   2. **Prefix inclusion.** The inclusion of an initial segment of length $q$ into one of length $c\ge q$. Initial-segment sums are full sums with the remaining summands set to $0$.
--   3. **Retained prefixes.** For an order embedding of retained candidates into all candidates, the sum of supported data over candidates before a retained one equals the sum over retained nodes before it.
